# Godot scene authoring (godot-cli)

## North star

Persist scene structure in `.tscn` the way a human would in the Godot editor. **Do not** use `load().instantiate()` in `_ready()` for static UI, HUDs, or level layout.

Read: `docs/agent_scene_authoring.md`

## Workflow

1. `catalog export --project-root .` or `catalog show <id> --json` when using project components
2. `scene node list <file.tscn> --json` before editing (`--project-root` optional)
3. Edit via CLI (`scene node add`, `scene instance add --catalog-id`, `scene apply`, etc.) — use `--project-root .`
4. `scene validate <file.tscn> --project-root .` after edits

## Prefer

| Task | Command |
|------|---------|
| New scene | `scene new --output … --root-name Main --root-type Node2D` |
| Add node | `scene node add … --parent /root/Main --name X --type Y` |
| Instance catalog entry | `scene instance add … --catalog-id ui/button --project-root .` |
| Batch edits | `scene plan … --intent intent.json` then `scene apply … --patch out.json` |
| Raw Godot control | `catalog show godot/ui/Button` → `scene node add --type Button` |

## Never

- Hand-edit `[node]` / `parent=` / `instance=` lines in `.tscn` when a CLI command exists
- `add_child(load("res://….tscn").instantiate())` for authored hierarchy
- Instance builtin catalog ids (`godot/…`) — they are document-only

